---
// Hero hierarchy diagram (Customer Journey → Four Capabilities → Growth Loop)
// is built inline here for V1 — three labeled boxes with connectors, simple
// enough not to warrant its own shared component yet.
const hierarchy = [
  { name: "Customer Journey", note: "where a constraint gets located" },
  { name: "Four Capabilities", note: "what the fix draws on" },
  { name: "Growth Loop", note: "how the fix gets measured" },
];
---

<section class="bg-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-teal-700">
      The Diagnostic Framework Behind Every Decision
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mt-4 max-w-4xl font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 md:text-6xl"
    >
      The framework behind every decision we make.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-600 md:text-xl">
      Before EverJourneys recommends anything, EverCompass finds out what's
      actually happening in your business — and what's getting in the way of
      where you're trying to go.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-slate-600">
      EverJourneys is the company. EverCompass is the framework it uses to
      diagnose a business and direct what needs to happen next — EverCompass
      diagnoses and directs; EverJourneys builds and improves what the diagnosis
      calls for. It works from what's observable in your business: how customers
      actually move through it, what's currently in place across your marketing
      and systems, and what the results show. A constraint gets identified by
      comparing that against where the business is actually trying to go — not by
      matching it to a generic playbook.
    </p>

    <figure class="mt-14">
      <figcaption
        class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate-400"
      >
        How EverCompass is structured
      </figcaption>
      <div
        class="mt-4 flex flex-col items-stretch gap-3 md:flex-row md:items-center"
      >
        {
          hierarchy.map((node, i) => (
            <>
              <div class="flex-1 rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-stone-50 p-5 text-center">
                <p class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">
                  {node.name}
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">{node.note}</p>
              </div>
              {i < hierarchy.length - 1 && (
                <span
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  class="mx-auto text-2xl text-teal-700 md:mx-0"
                >
                  <span class="hidden md:inline">&rarr;</span>
                  <span class="md:hidden">&darr;</span>
                </span>
              )}
            </>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">
        One flows into the next: the Customer Journey locates the constraint, the
        Four Capabilities supply the fix, and the Growth Loop measures and
        improves it.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
